 class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">unfold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">zi</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h1</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unfold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">zj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cast_sub</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">le_of_lt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hij</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">zpow_natCast</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xinv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hxinv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xinv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">unfold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xinv</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pow_succ'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sub_pos_iff_lt</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hij</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">conv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">change</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sub_add_comm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h4</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">add_one_sub_one</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h3</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inv_eq_iff_mul_eq_one</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hxinv</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- If j - i = 1, then x = e = x⁻¹ and x⁻¹ ∈ H.</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">conv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hij</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">change</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">le_iff_lt_or_eq</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hij</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hi</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">hi</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">add_tsub_cancel_left</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pow_one</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h3</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hxinv'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">one_eq_inv</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h3</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">rwa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h3</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hxinv'</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hx</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- Otherwise, xʲ⁻ⁱ⁻¹ = x⁻¹, and since j - i &gt; 1, x⁻¹ ∈ H.</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hi</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sub_pos_iff_lt</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hi</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sub_sub</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h4</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">hxinv</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unfold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xinv</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h_cyclx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h4</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">one_mem'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- doesn't work:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">--have h1 := inv_mem' h_nonempty</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 577875735,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael",
        "timestamp": 1772855887
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For your third question, you can extract the proof of <code>inv_mem</code> to its own theorem and reuse it... oh, you want your file to contain just one <code>example</code>? I am not sure if there is a clean way then. Why do you want this particular format? <code>example</code> is really just a way to quickly demonstrate something, not a recommended way to organize serious proof</p>",
        "id": 577876662,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1772856981
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's not so much that I want the file to contain just one example. What I don't want is for this particular example to begin <code>example ... : Subgroup G := by</code>, where as far as the declaration is concerned it's just a coincidence if the carrier of the subgroup demonstrated by the example happens to be <code>H</code>.</p>",
        "id": 577876766,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael",
        "timestamp": 1772857095
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm working on formalizing textbook problems, and I want to keep the declarations of <code>example</code>s as close to the way the problem is stated in the book as possible.</p>",
        "id": 577876896,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael",
        "timestamp": 1772857220
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(So I like <code>example ... : Subgroup G where carrier := H</code> as a reflection of \"<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.08125em;\">H</span></span></span></span> is a subgroup of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span>\", but I'm not as happy with <code>example ... : Subgroup G := by</code> which looks more like \"<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span> has a subgroup\".)</p>",
        "id": 577877230,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael",
        "timestamp": 1772857544
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh, I see. So it means you can accept this?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inv_mem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">....</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subgroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"n\">inv_mem'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inv_mem</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"n\">one_mem'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">also</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">use</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inv_mem</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 577877408,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1772857766
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, if the Subgroup fields are inaccessible to each other, that's probably what I'll do.</p>",
